module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SpecDividedPowerScheme

/-!
# Affine divided power quotients of an object of the crystalline site

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` and an object `(U, T, δ)` of the small
crystalline site `Cris(X/S)`.  Let `V ⊆ T` be an affine open and let `q : Γ(V, 𝒪_T) ⟶ R` be a
surjective homomorphism of divided power rings whose kernel is killed by the immersion
`U ↪ T` and which carries the divided power ideal of `T` onto the divided power ideal of `R`.
Then `U ∩ V ↪ Spec (R)` is again a divided power thickening, it is again an object of
`Cris(X/S)`, and it maps to `(U, T, δ)`.

This is the construction the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07J1] uses to test two maps out of the
sections of an object of `Cris(X/S)` over an affine open: a pair of divided power homomorphisms
`q, r : Γ(W, 𝒪_{T(1)}) ⟶ R` with `q` surjective and `R` presented as above determines two
morphisms of `Cris(X/S)` into `T(1)`, and the universal property of the product forces the two
to agree.  The payload of the file is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystallineProduct_affine_ext`, which packages exactly
that argument for a product presented by a limit binary fan.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections` — the morphism of divided power
  schemes `Spec (R) ⟶ T` attached to a divided power homomorphism out of the sections of `T`
  over an affine open.
* `Crystalline.affineQuotientImmersion` — the closed immersion `U ∩ V ⟶ Spec (R)` cut out by a
  surjective quotient `q : Γ(V, 𝒪_T) ⟶ R` that kills no more than `U ↪ T` does.
* `Crystalline.SchemeThickening.thickeningSourceMap` — the map on thickened schemes induced by a
  morphism of the ambient divided power schemes.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.affineQuotientCrystalline` and
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.affineQuotientCrystallineHom` — the object of
  `Cris(X/S)` presented by such a quotient, and its morphism to the original object.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystallineHomOfFactorization` — a morphism of
  `Cris(X/S)` built from a factorization of the ambient morphisms over a third object.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_of_appLE` — compatibility with divided powers on
  every open follows from compatibility on a single open `W` whose preimage is everything, as
  soon as the target's divided power ideal is generated from `W` on every affine open below it.
* `Crystalline.SchemeThickening.ideal_obj_eq_map` — the divided power ideal of a thickening is
  generated by its sections over any larger affine open.
* `Crystalline.affineQuotientImmersion_ker` and `Crystalline.affineQuotientImmersion_ideal_eq` —
  the quotient immersion cuts out exactly the divided power ideal of `Spec (R)`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystallineHom_ext_target` — a morphism of `Cris(X/S)`
  is determined by its ambient component.
* **`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystallineProduct_affine_ext`** — two divided power
  homomorphisms out of the sections of a self-product over an affine open agree as soon as one of
  them is a surjection presenting the divided power ideal and the two agree after composing with
  both projections.

## Implementation notes

The divided power scheme `Spec (R)` is
`Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme`, whose ideal is the quasi-coherent ideal
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop` generated by the ideal of `R`.  Identifying it with the kernel
of the quotient immersion is therefore a statement about `Scheme.ker_of_isAffine` rather than
about a sheaf-theoretic kernel, which is why `affineQuotientImmersion_ker` is proved first and
`affineQuotientImmersion_ideal_eq` is read off from it on affine opens.

Only the inclusion `J_T ⊆ ker(𝒪_T → 𝒪_U)`, recorded by
`Crystalline.SchemeThickening.immersion_app_eq_zero_of_mem`, is needed for
`Crystalline.SchemeThickening.ker_le_comp`; the equality of the two ideals over a general open is
never used.

No tag attribute is placed in this file: it is infrastructure for the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 07J1] and states none of its assertions.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07I3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07I3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07I6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07I6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07J1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07J1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Crystalline

namespace DividedPowerScheme

/-- A morphism compatible with the divided powers over a big open `W` is compatible with them
over every affine open below `W` on which the ideal is generated by its sections over `W`. -/
theorem isDPMorphism_app_of_appLE
    (D E : DividedPowerScheme.{u}) (f : D.scheme ⟶ E.scheme)
    (W : E.scheme.Opens) (hW : ⊤ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (hI : ∀ (V : E.scheme.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ W), E.ideal.obj (op V.1) =
      Ideal.map (E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom
        (E.ideal.obj (op W)))
    (hf : (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op W)).IsDPMorphism
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op ⊤)) (f.appLE W ⊤ hW).hom)
    (V : E.scheme.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ W) :
    (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op V.1)).IsDPMorphism
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1))) (f.app V.1).hom := by
  apply DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.of_comp
    (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op W)) _ _
    (E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom
    (f.app V.1).hom (hI V hVW)
    (E.dividedPowers.naturality (homOfLE hVW).op)
  have hcomp := (D.dividedPowers.naturality
    (homOfLE (le_top : f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ≤ ⊤)).op).comp _ hf
  have hc : (f.app V.1).hom.comp
      (E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom =
      (D.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ≤ ⊤)).op).hom.comp
        (f.appLE W ⊤ hW).hom := by
    have hc' : E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op ≫ f.app V.1 =
        f.appLE W ⊤ hW ≫ D.scheme.presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (le_top : f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ≤ ⊤)).op := by
      rw [f.app_eq_appLE, Scheme.Hom.map_appLE, Scheme.Hom.appLE_map]
    exact congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom hc'
  exact hc ▸ hcomp

/-- Under the hypotheses of `isDPMorphism_app_of_appLE`, the morphism maps the divided power
ideal of `E` over any open `U` into that of `D` over `f ⁻¹ᵁ U`. -/
theorem app_mem_ideal_of_appLE
    (D E : DividedPowerScheme.{u}) (f : D.scheme ⟶ E.scheme)
    (W : E.scheme.Opens) (hW : ⊤ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (hI : ∀ (V : E.scheme.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ W), E.ideal.obj (op V.1) =
      Ideal.map (E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom
        (E.ideal.obj (op W)))
    (hf : (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op W)).IsDPMorphism
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op ⊤)) (f.appLE W ⊤ hW).hom)
    (U : E.scheme.Opens) (x : Γ(E.scheme, U)) (hx : x ∈ E.ideal.obj (op U)) :
    f.app U x ∈ D.ideal.obj (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) := by
  apply D.ideal.isSheaf
  intro z hz
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hzV, hVUW⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset
    (X := E.scheme) (U := U ⊓ W) (show f z ∈ U ⊓ W from ⟨hz, hW trivial⟩)
  let i : V ⟶ U := homOfLE (hVUW.trans inf_le_left)
  let j : f ⁻¹ᵁ V ⟶ f ⁻¹ᵁ U := (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map f.base).map i
  refine ⟨f ⁻¹ᵁ V, j, ?_, hzV⟩
  change D.scheme.presheaf.map j.op (f.app U x) ∈ D.ideal.obj (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ V))
  have hnat := congrArg (fun g => g x) (f.naturality i.op)
  exact hnat ▸ (isDPMorphism_app_of_appLE D E f W hW hI hf ⟨V, hV⟩
    (hVUW.trans inf_le_right)).ideal_comp (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (E.ideal.map_mem i.op hx))

/-- **Compatibility with divided powers may be checked on a single big open.**  Let `D`, `E` be
divided power schemes and `f : D.scheme ⟶ E.scheme` a morphism whose preimage of an open `W` of
`E` is everything.  If the divided power ideal of `E` on every affine open below `W` is generated
by its sections over `W`, and `f` is compatible with the divided powers over `W`, then it is
compatible over every open `U`. -/
theorem isDPMorphism_of_appLE
    (D E : DividedPowerScheme.{u}) (f : D.scheme ⟶ E.scheme)
    (W : E.scheme.Opens) (hW : ⊤ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (hI : ∀ (V : E.scheme.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ W), E.ideal.obj (op V.1) =
      Ideal.map (E.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom
        (E.ideal.obj (op W)))
    (hf : (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op W)).IsDPMorphism
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op ⊤)) (f.appLE W ⊤ hW).hom)
    (U : E.scheme.Opens) :
    (E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U)).IsDPMorphism
      (D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ U))) (f.app U).hom := by
  have hideal := app_mem_ideal_of_appLE D E f W hW hI hf U
  refine ⟨Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hideal, ?_⟩
  intro n x hx
  let ι := {V : E.scheme.affineOpens // V.1 ≤ U ⊓ W}
  let B (V : ι) : D.scheme.Opens := f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1.1
  let i (V : ι) : V.1.1 ⟶ U := homOfLE (V.2.trans inf_le_left)
  let j (V : ι) : B V ⟶ f ⁻¹ᵁ U := (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map f.base).map (i V)
  refine D.scheme.sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq' B (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) j ?_ _ _ ?_
  · intro z hz
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hzV, hVUW⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset
      (X := E.scheme) (U := U ⊓ W) (show f z ∈ U ⊓ W from ⟨hz, hW trivial⟩)
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hVUW⟩, hzV⟩
  · intro V
    have hnat (a : Γ(E.scheme, U)) :
        f.app V.1.1 (E.scheme.presheaf.map (i V).op a) =
        D.scheme.presheaf.map (j V).op (f.app U a) :=
      congrArg (fun g => g a) (f.naturality (i V).op)
    change D.scheme.presheaf.map (j V).op
        ((D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ U))).dpow n (f.app U x)) =
      D.scheme.presheaf.map (j V).op
        (f.app U ((E.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op U)).dpow n x))
    refine (D.dividedPowers.naturality (j V).op).map_dpow (hideal x hx) |>.trans ?_
    refine (congrArg ((D.dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op (B V))).dpow n) (hnat x).symm).trans ?_
    refine (isDPMorphism_app_of_appLE D E f W hW hI hf V.1
        (V.2.trans inf_le_right)).dpow_comp _
      (E.ideal.map_mem (i V).op hx) |>.trans ?_
    exact (congrArg (fun a => f.app V.1.1 a)
      ((E.dividedPowers.naturality (i V).op).map_dpow hx).symm).trans (hnat _)

/-- On `⊤` the chosen divided powers of `Spec (A, I, γ)` restrict to `γ`, spelled as a statement
about the divided power structure of the scheme rather than about a morphism of divided power
rings. -/
theorem specDividedPowerSchemeUnit_isDPMorphism (A : DividedPowerRing.{u}) :
    A.dividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
      ((specDividedPowerScheme A).dividedPowers.dividedPowers (op ⊤))
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom :=
  (specDividedPowerSchemeUnit A).isDPMorphism

end DividedPowerScheme

/-- **The kernel of `Spec f` on global sections is the image of the kernel of `f`.**  Both
`Scheme.ΓSpecIso` isomorphisms are used to move the kernel across the `Γ`-`Spec` adjunction. -/
theorem ker_specMap_appTop {R T : CommRingCat.{u}} (f : R ⟶ T) :
    RingHom.ker (Spec.map f).appTop.hom =
      (RingHom.ker f.hom).map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).inv.hom := by
  calc
    RingHom.ker (Spec.map f).appTop.hom =
        RingHom.ker ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso T).hom.hom.comp (Spec.map f).appTop.hom) :=
      (RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _
        (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (Scheme.ΓSpecIso T).hom).1).symm
    _ = RingHom.ker (f.hom.comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).hom.hom) :=
      congrArg RingHom.ker (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (Scheme.ΓSpecIso_naturality f))
    _ = (RingHom.ker f.hom).comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).hom.hom := (RingHom.comap_ker _ _).symm
    _ = (RingHom.ker f.hom).map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).inv.hom :=
      (Ideal.map_comap_of_equiv (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv).symm

namespace SchemeThickening

/-- **The divided power ideal of a thickening is generated from any larger affine open.**  On
affine opens the ideal is the one of the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data of the immersion, which
is generated by its sections over a larger affine open. -/
theorem ideal_obj_eq_map (E : SchemeThickening.{u})
    (V W : E.target.scheme.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ W.1) :
    E.target.ideal.obj (op V.1) =
      Ideal.map (E.target.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op).hom
        (E.target.ideal.obj (op W.1)) := by
  rw [E.ideal_eq_ker, E.ideal_eq_ker]
  exact (E.immersion.ker.map_ideal hVW).symm

end SchemeThickening

/-- The canonical map from the sections of an affine open to the global sections of its spectrum
is the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. -/
theorem fromSpec_appLE (X : Scheme.{u}) (V : X.affineOpens) :
    V.2.fromSpec.appLE V.1 ⊤ V.2.fromSpec_preimage_self.ge =
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(X, V.1)).inv := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE, V.2.fromSpec_app_self, Category.assoc,
    ← (Spec Γ(X, V.1)).presheaf.map_comp]
  have hi : (eqToHom V.2.fromSpec_preimage_self).op ≫
      (homOfLE V.2.fromSpec_preimage_self.ge).op = 𝟙 (op ⊤) := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  rw [hi, (Spec Γ(X, V.1)).presheaf.map_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- `Spec` of a ring map into the sections over an affine open, followed by `fromSpec`, lands
inside that affine open. -/
theorem le_preimage_fromSpec_comp {X : Scheme.{u}} (V : X.affineOpens) {R : CommRingCat.{u}}
    (φ : Γ(X, V.1) ⟶ R) : ⊤ ≤ (Spec.map φ ≫ V.2.fromSpec) ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage, V.2.fromSpec_preimage_self]
  exact (Scheme.Hom.preimage_top _).ge

/-- On sections over the affine open, `Spec φ` followed by `fromSpec` is `φ` itself. -/
theorem appLE_fromSpec_comp {X : Scheme.{u}} (V : X.affineOpens) {R : CommRingCat.{u}}
    (φ : Γ(X, V.1) ⟶ R) :
    (Spec.map φ ≫ V.2.fromSpec).appLE V.1 ⊤ (le_preimage_fromSpec_comp V φ) =
      φ ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).inv := by
  have h := Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE (Spec.map φ) V.2.fromSpec V.1 ⊤ ⊤
    V.2.fromSpec_preimage_self.ge (by simp)
  rw [fromSpec_appLE X V] at h
  exact h.symm.trans (Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality _).symm

namespace SchemeThickening

/-- **The morphism of divided power schemes `Spec (R) ⟶ T` attached to a divided power
homomorphism out of the sections of `T` over an affine open `V`.**  The underlying morphism of
schemes is `Spec` of the homomorphism followed by `IsAffineOpen.fromSpec`; compatibility with the
divided powers on every open follows from compatibility over `V` by
`Crystalline.DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_of_appLE`. -/
def dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (f : E.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R) :
    DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme R ⟶ E.target := by
  refine ⟨_, DividedPowerScheme.isDPMorphism_of_appLE _ _ _ V.1
    (le_preimage_fromSpec_comp V (CommRingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom))
    (fun W hWV ↦ ideal_obj_eq_map E W V hWV) ?_⟩
  exact appLE_fromSpec_comp V (CommRingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom) ▸
    (DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerSchemeUnit_isDPMorphism R).comp _ f.isDPMorphism

/-- The underlying morphism of schemes of
`Crystalline.SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections`. -/
@[simp]
theorem dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections_hom
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (f : E.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R) :
    (dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections E V R f).hom =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom) ≫ V.2.fromSpec := rfl

end SchemeThickening

/-- **The closed immersion `U ∩ V ⟶ Spec (R)` cut out by a surjective quotient
`q : Γ(V, 𝒪_T) ⟶ R`.**  The hypothesis `hk` says that `q` kills no more than the immersion of the
thickening does, so the immersion factors through `q`. -/
def affineQuotientImmersion
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom) :
    (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toScheme ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R) :=
  (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
    (q.liftOfSurjective hq ⟨(E.immersion.app V.1).hom, hk⟩))

/-- The quotient immersion followed by `Spec q` composed into `T` is the immersion of the
thickening restricted to `V`. -/
theorem affineQuotientImmersion_comp
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom) :
    affineQuotientImmersion E V q hq hk ≫
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q) ≫ V.2.fromSpec) =
      (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι ≫ E.immersion := by
  unfold affineQuotientImmersion
  rw [Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc (Spec.map _) (Spec.map _), ← Spec.map_comp]
  have hc : CommRingCat.ofHom q ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom
      (q.liftOfSurjective hq ⟨(E.immersion.app V.1).hom, hk⟩) = E.immersion.app V.1 :=
    CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.liftOfSurjective_comp _ _ _)
  rw [hc, ← Category.assoc, Scheme.Opens.toSpecΓ_naturality,
    Category.assoc, V.2.toSpecΓ_fromSpec, morphismRestrict_ι]

/-- The quotient immersion is a closed immersion: it is an isomorphism followed by `Spec` of a
surjection. -/
theorem affineQuotientImmersion_isClosedImmersion
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom) :
    IsClosedImmersion (affineQuotientImmersion E V q hq hk) := by
  let r := q.liftOfSurjective hq ⟨(E.immersion.app V.1).hom, hk⟩
  have hr : Function.Surjective r := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := E.immersion.app_surjective V.1 V.2 x
    exact ⟨q y, (RingHom.liftOfSurjective_comp_apply _ _ _ _).trans hy⟩
  have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom r)) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ hr
  have : IsAffine (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toScheme := V.2.preimage E.immersion
  have : IsIso (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsIso (V.2.preimage E.immersion).isoSpec.hom)
  change IsClosedImmersion ((E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom r))
  infer_instance

/-- The quotient immersion is surjective on points, because the thickening is. -/
theorem affineQuotientImmersion_surjective
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom) :
    Function.Surjective (affineQuotientImmersion E V q hq hk) := by
  let g := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q) ≫ V.2.fromSpec
  have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q)) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ hq
  have : IsOpenImmersion V.2.fromSpec := V.2.isOpenImmersion_fromSpec
  have hg : Function.Injective g :=
    V.2.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.injective.comp
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q)).isClosedEmbedding.injective
  intro x
  have hx : g x ∈ V.1 :=
    V.2.range_fromSpec.le ⟨Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q) x, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := E.isThickening.2 (g x)
  have hzV : z ∈ E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 := by
    change E.immersion z ∈ V.1
    rwa [hz]
  exact ⟨⟨z, hzV⟩, hg <|
    (congrArg (fun f => f ⟨z, hzV⟩) (affineQuotientImmersion_comp E V q hq hk)).trans hz⟩

/-- **The quotient immersion cuts out the divided power ideal of `Spec (R)`.**  On global
sections its kernel is the image of the ideal of `R`, by the factorization of the immersion
through `q`. -/
theorem affineQuotientImmersion_ker
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (R : DividedPowerRing.{u}) (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q (E.target.ideal.obj (op V.1))) :
    (affineQuotientImmersion E V q hq hk).ker =
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (R.ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv.hom) := by
  let r := q.liftOfSurjective hq ⟨(E.immersion.app V.1).hom, hk⟩
  have hr : RingHom.ker r = R.ideal := by
    rw [hI, E.ideal_eq_ker, Scheme.Hom.ker_apply]
    have he : (RingHom.ker r).comap q = RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom := by
      rw [RingHom.comap_ker, RingHom.liftOfSurjective_comp]
    rw [← he]
    exact (Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective q hq (RingHom.ker r)).symm
  have : IsAffine (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toScheme := V.2.preimage E.immersion
  have : IsIso (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsIso (V.2.preimage E.immersion).isoSpec.hom)
  have : IsIso (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ.appTop :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsIso ((E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ.app ⊤))
  rw [Scheme.ker_of_isAffine]
  congr 1
  change RingHom.ker ((E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ ≫
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom r)).appTop.hom = _
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop]
  change RingHom.ker ((E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ.appTop.hom.comp
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom r)).appTop.hom) = _
  rw [RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toSpecΓ.appTop).1]
  exact (ker_specMap_appTop (CommRingCat.ofHom r)).trans
    (congrArg (fun I : Ideal R => I.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv.hom) hr)

/-- On an affine open, the divided power ideal of `Spec (R)` is the defining ideal of the
quotient immersion.  This is the `ideal_eq_ker` field of the thickening presented by the
quotient. -/
theorem affineQuotientImmersion_ideal_eq
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (R : DividedPowerRing.{u}) (q : Γ(E.target.scheme, V.1) →+* R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hk : RingHom.ker q ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q (E.target.ideal.obj (op V.1)))
    (W : (DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme R).scheme.affineOpens) :
    (DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme R).ideal.obj (op W.1) =
      (affineQuotientImmersion E V q hq hk).ker.ideal W :=
  (DividedPowerScheme.idealSheafAsSubmodule_obj_affine _ W).trans
    (congrArg (fun d : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).IdealSheafData => d.ideal W)
      (affineQuotientImmersion_ker E V R q hq hk hI).symm)

namespace SchemeThickening

/-- **The defining ideal of a thickening pulls back into the defining ideal of another.**  If
`f : D.target ⟶ E.target` is a morphism of the ambient divided power schemes, the kernel of the
immersion of `E` is contained in the kernel of the immersion of `D` composed with `f`. -/
theorem ker_le_comp (D E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (f : D.target ⟶ E.target) :
    E.immersion.ker ≤ (D.immersion ≫ f.hom).ker := by
  apply Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_ofIdeals_iff.mpr
  intro U x hx
  have hxi : x ∈ E.target.ideal.obj (op U.1) := (E.ideal_eq_ker U).symm ▸ hx
  have hmem := (f.compatible U.1).ideal_comp (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hxi)
  change f.hom.app U.1 x ∈ D.target.ideal.obj (op (f.hom ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) at hmem
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, Scheme.Hom.comp_app]
  exact D.immersion_app_eq_zero_of_mem _ _ hmem

/-- **The map on thickened schemes induced by a morphism of the ambient divided power
schemes.**  It is the lift of `D.immersion ≫ f.hom` through the closed immersion of `E`. -/
def thickeningSourceMap
    (D E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (f : D.target ⟶ E.target) :
    D.source ⟶ E.source :=
  IsClosedImmersion.lift E.immersion (D.immersion ≫ f.hom) (ker_le_comp D E f)

/-- The induced map on thickened schemes makes the square of immersions commute. -/
theorem thickeningSourceMap_comp
    (D E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (f : D.target ⟶ E.target) :
    thickeningSourceMap D E f ≫ E.immersion = D.immersion ≫ f.hom :=
  IsClosedImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _

end SchemeThickening

/-- **The divided power thickening of schemes presented by a surjective divided power quotient
of the sections over an affine open.** -/
def affineQuotientSchemeThickening
    (E : SchemeThickening.{u}) (V : E.target.scheme.affineOpens) (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (q : E.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q.toRingHom)
    (hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom ≤ RingHom.ker (E.immersion.app V.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q.toRingHom (E.target.ideal.obj (op V.1))) :
    SchemeThickening.{u} where
  source := (E.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).toScheme
  target := DividedPowerScheme.specDividedPowerScheme R
  immersion := affineQuotientImmersion E V q.toRingHom hq hk
  isThickening := ⟨affineQuotientImmersion_isClosedImmersion _ _ _ _ _,
    affineQuotientImmersion_surjective _ _ _ _ _⟩
  ideal_eq_ker := affineQuotientImmersion_ideal_eq _ _ _ _ _ _ hI

namespace GlobalCrystallineSituation

/-- The quotient immersion is a morphism over the divided power base. -/
theorem affineQuotient_over_base
    {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (E : CrystallineThickening S)
    (V : E.obj.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens) (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (q : E.obj.thickening.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q.toRingHom)
    (hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom ≤ RingHom.ker (E.obj.thickening.immersion.app V.1).hom) :
    affineQuotientImmersion E.obj.thickening V q.toRingHom hq hk ≫
        (SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections E.obj.thickening V R q ≫
          E.obj.toBase).hom =
      ((E.obj.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι ≫ E.obj.toX) ≫ sourceToBase S := by
  refine Eq.trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun φ ↦ φ ≫ E.obj.toBase.hom)
    (affineQuotientImmersion_comp E.obj.thickening V q.toRingHom hq hk)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Category.assoc _ _ _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun φ ↦ (E.obj.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι ≫ φ)
    E.obj.over_base) ?_
  exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm

/-- **The object of `Cris(X/S)` presented by a surjective divided power quotient of the sections
over an affine open.**  The thickened scheme is the part of `U` lying over `V`, the ambient
divided power scheme is `Spec (R)`, and the two structure morphisms are inherited from `E`. -/
def affineQuotientCrystalline
    (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) (E : CrystallineThickening S)
    (V : E.obj.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens) (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (q : E.obj.thickening.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q.toRingHom)
    (hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom ≤ RingHom.ker (E.obj.thickening.immersion.app V.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q.toRingHom (E.obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op V.1))) :
    CrystallineThickening S := by
  refine ⟨{
    thickening := affineQuotientSchemeThickening E.obj.thickening V R q hq hk hI
    toBase := SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections E.obj.thickening V R q ≫
      E.obj.toBase
    toX := (E.obj.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι ≫ E.obj.toX
    over_base := affineQuotient_over_base E V R q hq hk }, ?_⟩
  have : IsOpenImmersion E.obj.toX := E.property
  change IsOpenImmersion ((E.obj.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι ≫ E.obj.toX)
  infer_instance

/-- The morphism of `Cris(X/S)` from the object presented by a surjective divided power quotient
to the original object. -/
def affineQuotientCrystallineHom
    (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) (E : CrystallineThickening S)
    (V : E.obj.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens) (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (q : E.obj.thickening.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op V.1) ⟶ R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q.toRingHom)
    (hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom ≤ RingHom.ker (E.obj.thickening.immersion.app V.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q.toRingHom (E.obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op V.1))) :
    affineQuotientCrystalline S E V R q hq hk hI ⟶ E :=
  ⟨{
    sourceHom := (E.obj.thickening.immersion ⁻¹ᵁ V.1).ι
    targetHom := SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections E.obj.thickening V R q
    immersion_naturality := affineQuotientImmersion_comp _ _ _ _ _
    base_naturality := rfl
    toX_naturality := rfl }⟩

/-- **A morphism of `Cris(X/S)` built from a factorization over a third object.**  Given
`p : E ⟶ A`, `q : D ⟶ A` and a morphism `f` of the ambient divided power schemes with
`f ≫ p = q` on ambient schemes, the lift of `f` through the immersion of `E` makes `f` into a
morphism `D ⟶ E`. -/
def crystallineHomOfFactorization
    {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {D E A : CrystallineThickening S}
    (p : E ⟶ A) (q : D ⟶ A) (f : D.obj.thickening.target ⟶ E.obj.thickening.target)
    (hf : f ≫ p.hom.targetHom = q.hom.targetHom) : D ⟶ E := by
  let a := SchemeThickening.thickeningSourceMap D.obj.thickening E.obj.thickening f
  have ha : a ≫ p.hom.sourceHom = q.hom.sourceHom := by
    apply (cancel_mono A.obj.thickening.immersion).mp
    rw [Category.assoc, ← p.hom.immersion_naturality, ← Category.assoc,
      SchemeThickening.thickeningSourceMap_comp, Category.assoc,
      ← DividedPowerScheme.Hom.comp_hom, hf, q.hom.immersion_naturality]
  refine ⟨{
    sourceHom := a
    targetHom := f
    immersion_naturality := (SchemeThickening.thickeningSourceMap_comp _ _ _).symm
    base_naturality := ?_
    toX_naturality := ?_ }⟩
  · rw [← p.hom.base_naturality, ← Category.assoc, hf, q.hom.base_naturality]
  · rw [← p.hom.toX_naturality, ← Category.assoc, ha, q.hom.toX_naturality]

/-- **A morphism of `Cris(X/S)` is determined by its ambient component.**  The map on thickened
schemes is determined by it, because the immersion of the target is a monomorphism. -/
theorem crystallineHom_ext_target
    {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {D E : CrystallineThickening S}
    (f g : D ⟶ E) (h : f.hom.targetHom = g.hom.targetHom) : f = g := by
  apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
  apply Thickening.Hom.ext
  · apply (cancel_mono E.obj.thickening.immersion).mp
    rw [← f.hom.immersion_naturality, ← g.hom.immersion_naturality, h]
  · exact h

end GlobalCrystallineSituation

/-- Two maps out of the sections over an affine open that agree after restriction along a
morphism induce the same composite out of the spectrum of those sections. -/
theorem fromSpec_comp_eq_of_comp_appLE_eq
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (V : X.affineOpens) (W : Y.affineOpens) (hVW : V.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W.1)
    (R : CommRingCat.{u}) (q r : Γ(X, V.1) ⟶ R)
    (h : f.appLE W.1 V.1 hVW ≫ q = f.appLE W.1 V.1 hVW ≫ r) :
    (Spec.map q ≫ V.2.fromSpec) ≫ f = (Spec.map r ≫ V.2.fromSpec) ≫ f := by
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← W.2.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f V.2 hVW,
    ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc,
    ← Spec.map_comp, ← Spec.map_comp, h]

namespace GlobalCrystallineSituation

/-- **Two divided power homomorphisms out of the sections of a self-product over an affine open
agree once they agree on both projections.**  Let `D` be a product of `B` with itself in
`Cris(X/S)`, presented by a limit binary fan with projections `pr₀, pr₁`, let `W` be an affine
open of the ambient scheme of `D` lying over an affine open `V` of the ambient scheme of `B`
along both projections, and let `q, r : Γ(W, 𝒪) ⟶ R` be divided power homomorphisms with `q`
surjective, killing no more than the immersion of `D` does and presenting the divided power ideal
of `R`.  Then `q` and `r` agree as soon as they agree after composing with the two projections:
both present morphisms of `Cris(X/S)` into `D`, and the universal property of the product forces
those to coincide. -/
theorem crystallineProduct_affine_ext {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}
    {B D : CrystallineThickening S} {pr₀ pr₁ : D ⟶ B} (h : IsLimit (BinaryFan.mk pr₀ pr₁))
    (V : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (W : D.obj.thickening.target.scheme.affineOpens)
    (h₀ : W.1 ≤ pr₀.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)
    (h₁ : W.1 ≤ pr₁.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)
    (R : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    (q r : D.obj.thickening.target.dividedPowers.toDividedPowerRing (op W.1) ⟶ R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q.toRingHom)
    (hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom ≤ RingHom.ker (D.obj.thickening.immersion.app W.1).hom)
    (hI : R.ideal = Ideal.map q.toRingHom (D.obj.thickening.target.ideal.obj (op W.1)))
    (hfirst : q.toRingHom.comp (pr₀.hom.targetHom.hom.appLE V.1 W.1 h₀).hom =
      r.toRingHom.comp (pr₀.hom.targetHom.hom.appLE V.1 W.1 h₀).hom)
    (hsecond : q.toRingHom.comp (pr₁.hom.targetHom.hom.appLE V.1 W.1 h₁).hom =
      r.toRingHom.comp (pr₁.hom.targetHom.hom.appLE V.1 W.1 h₁).hom) :
    q.toRingHom = r.toRingHom := by
  let Q := affineQuotientCrystalline S D W R q hq hk hI
  let a : Q ⟶ D := affineQuotientCrystallineHom S D W R q hq hk hI
  let b : Q.obj.thickening.target ⟶ D.obj.thickening.target :=
    SchemeThickening.dividedPowerHomOfAffineSections D.obj.thickening W R r
  have hcomp₀ : b ≫ pr₀.hom.targetHom = (a ≫ pr₀).hom.targetHom :=
    DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext <| fromSpec_comp_eq_of_comp_appLE_eq _ W V h₀ _ _ _
      (CommRingCat.hom_ext hfirst.symm)
  have hcomp₁ : b ≫ pr₁.hom.targetHom = (a ≫ pr₁).hom.targetHom :=
    DividedPowerScheme.Hom.ext <| fromSpec_comp_eq_of_comp_appLE_eq _ W V h₁ _ _ _
      (CommRingCat.hom_ext hsecond.symm)
  let c : Q ⟶ D := crystallineHomOfFactorization pr₀ (a ≫ pr₀) b hcomp₀
  have hc : c = a := by
    refine BinaryFan.IsLimit.hom_ext h ?_ ?_
    · rw [BinaryFan.mk_fst]
      exact crystallineHom_ext_target _ _ hcomp₀
    · rw [BinaryFan.mk_snd]
      exact crystallineHom_ext_target _ _ hcomp₁
  have hg : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom r.toRingHom) ≫ W.2.fromSpec =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q.toRingHom) ≫ W.2.fromSpec :=
    congrArg (fun φ : Q ⟶ D => φ.hom.targetHom.hom) hc
  have : IsOpenImmersion W.2.fromSpec := W.2.isOpenImmersion_fromSpec
  exact (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom
    (Spec.map_injective ((cancel_mono W.2.fromSpec).mp hg))).symm

end GlobalCrystallineSituation

end Crystalline

